{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 7, :comments ["<b>And the work was enough.</b> For all the work that they had to do, and still there would be left over from it. And by way of the plain sense (peshat), it says: the work — they had enough of it for what was needed. And I ask here: why did the verse need to state this, seeing that it already mentioned above that the people brought more than enough for the work that YHWH had commanded to do, and it was left over — and from there I would already understand the sufficiency and the surplus." "<b>And it is possible</b> to say that this verse alludes to us that the Mishkan below corresponds to the Sanctuary (בהמ\"ק) on high; and so the Midrash states: the Sanctuary below corresponds to the Sanctuary on high, as it is said (Exodus 15:17): ״מכון לשבתך פעלת ה' מקדש ה' כוננו ידיך״." "<b>And you already</b> know that the name YHWH is the Sanctuary (בהמ\"ק) on high, and therefore the Midrash used the expression 'heikhal.' And the sense of the verse will be: 'and the work on high was enough and more than enough for all the work, to do it' — that is, corresponding to all the work below that was incumbent upon them to do. And you already know that from there comes the sustenance and provision for the Sanctuary below and for the totality of the world, the supernal and the lower. And therefore the verse mentioned the expression 'work' (מלאכה) twice: for that on high it used the expression of being (הויה), and for that below it used the expression of making (עשיה). And understand this."], :book :exodus, :voice :rabbeinu-bahya, :lang :en, :chapter 36, :notes {1 "בהמ\"ק read as abbreviation for בית המקדש (the Sanctuary/Temple)."}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T14:07:37.874135813Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}